  "notes": "The fastest notated band in this batch (152–160) under the most static harmony, which is the combination the research describes: \"a two-chord minor bed with a single bell/pluck figure — harmony is nearly static\", and the energy is in the flow rather than in the beat. \"The vocal supplies all melodic movement with wide unpredictable leaps and non-lexical syllables\" is what the melody block is: `intervals.leap` 0.4 and `octaveJumpProb` 0.4 are the highest in the batch by a distance, against `trinidad-james` — the other minimal high-motif entry here — at 0.12 and 0.04. Two records that look alike on paper (2-bar loop, tiny pitch set, no pad, cold open) and are opposites in the only place it matters. \"Long sustained tonic 808 with an occasional octave drop; no glide-heavy writing\" is `slideProb` 0.12 with `P8` as the only interval, and `sustain: legato` over a low narrow register. \"Extremely sparse mid-range\" is why nothing is authored between the 808's ceiling at 27 and the motif's floor at 80. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium`: the research says medium-high on the single and medium overall, and one record is the whole basis. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the kick's single syncopated 16th as a `syncopation` number, and the family weights — the research names \"two-chord\" without naming which two, so `i–VI` and `i–VII` are both authored at equal weight rather than one being chosen. ⚠ **A register here spanned less than an octave and has been widened.** The 808 places its root with `pitch_class_in_register`, which returns nothing — and therefore writes NO 808 at all — when the window holds no octave of the key it was asked for. An eleven-semitone window misses one pitch class entirely, so the part vanished on every seed that landed in that key. The centre of the authored range is unchanged. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
